+// UncertainLivenessReporter is implemented by providers whose liveness
+// checks are backed by a cache that can itself fail to observe current
+// state (e.g. a subprocess snapshot that times out or is killed under
+// load). LastObservationUncertain reports whether the most recent
+// IsRunning/ObserveLiveness answer for ANY session might reflect "could not
+// read live state right now" rather than a confirmed result.
+//
+// ga-ebbr2t: a reconciler that treats a negative IsRunning as proof of death
+// immediately after starting a session can race a failed state-cache
+// refresh -- the refresh error collapses into the same false value as a
+// genuine "not running," and the reconciler then attempts a destructive
+// fresh-start against a session that never actually died. Callers about to
+// treat a negative liveness answer as confirmed death should check this
+// first and, when true, defer to the next tick instead of acting.
+type UncertainLivenessReporter interface {
+	LastObservationUncertain() bool
+}
